{title: He Aint Never Done Me Nothin But Good}
{key: G}

{comment: Chorus}
[G]He ain't never [C]done me nothin'
[G]Done me nothin' [C]but good
Nothin' but good
Ooo, ooo ooo,
[G]He ain't never [C]done me nothin'
[G]Done me nothin' but [C]good,
[G]Nothin' but [C]good.

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]Job was a righteous man, the [C]devil couldn't doubt it.
[G]He surely loved the Saviour, there was [C]no doubt about it.
But [G]Satan cursed his body from his feet to his [C]head;
[G]Told him all his children and his [C]cattle we dead.
[G]Job's wife said, "Why don't you [C]curse your God and die?"
But [G]Job said, "Woman, you're [C]speakin' like a foolish child".

{comment: Verse 2}
I [G]gave my heart to Jesus and I [C]took Him as my Saviour.
I [G]cast my lots with the chosen ones and [C]I started out to Heaven.
[G]Soon I was forsaken and my friends left one by [C]one;
But the [G]good Lord walked beside me and He [C]never left me alone.
[G]He feed me when I was hungry, He[C] cheered me when I was sad.
[G]He has been the dearest [C]friend this child has ever had.

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]History tells of Polycarp who [C]died for the gospel's sake.
They [G]built a fire around him and they [C]tied him to a stake.
[G]But the fire could not comsume him, So they [C]pierced him with a sword.
The [G]fire went out, the blood ran down, But [C]still he praised the Lord.
[G]All my years I've served Him, He ain't [C]done me nothin' but good.
[G]Well, I won't repent and I won't recant, Just [C]tell me why I should.
